error[E0277]: `std::option::Option<i64>` has no storage of its own type, so a parameter cannot borrow one
 --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_option.rs:5:1
  |
5 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this parameter is taken by reference
  |
  = help: the trait `Borrowable<__R>` is not implemented for `std::option::Option<i64>`
  = note: a borrowed aggregate crosses as its projection: where `std::option::Option<i64>` is a `#[derive(TyArg)] #[projection]` aggregate, write `std::option::Option<i64>Ref<'_>`, or `std::option::Option<i64>Mut<'_>` for a struct and `std::option::Option<i64>Mut<'_, Rt>` for an enum (RFC-0050 rule 6).
  = note: an Option has no storage of its own type to borrow: `None` is one value and `Some(v)` is `v`'s own value, so nothing behind a reference is shaped like an `Option<T>`. Take `Option<&T>`, or the option by value.
  = note: a Rust slice is not one of the language's types: take `Slice<T, Shared, Rt>`, the language's `&[T]` (RFC-0047).
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Borrowable<Rt>`:
            `()` implements `Borrowable<__Rt>`
            `Arr<T, N>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `ChosenNth<N>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Erased<R, T>` implements `Borrowable<R>`
            `Nth<acvus_extern::kind::Type, N>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Spec<T>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `Vec<T>` implements `Borrowable<Rt>`
            `bool` implements `Borrowable<__Rt>`
          and $N others
  = note: required for `ByRef<std::option::Option<i64>, acvus_extern::Shared>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
  = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
